Design: BST<T> with comparator (a, b) => number. insert, has, delete, size getter, [Symbol.iterator]() generator doing iterative in-order with explicit stack.

For the injectable counter of stack pushes: allow constructor option like `onStackPush?: () => void` or a second constructor arg `options`. The iterator pushes nodes onto an explicit stack; each push calls the counter. Test: build 10000-node tree, get iterator, take 3 items via next(), assert counter < some small bound (e.g., ≤ ~50), proving laziness (no full materialization which would be 10000).

